# RUNBOOK.md and REVIEW.md both name CODEOWNERS as part of this tool's control
# story -- "a signed commit behind CODEOWNERS proves identity and independent
# review" -- and the file did not exist. A control the documentation claims and
# the repository lacks is worse than no claim: it is the failure mode this tool
# was built to find, in its own tree.
#
# CODEOWNERS only has teeth with branch protection requiring review from code
# owners. Without that it is advisory, and RUNBOOK.md:180 already says so.

*                           @ianshank

# The three documents a release binds by hash. `archtrace release` signs these;
# a change here is a change to what was approved.
/engagements/               @ianshank
/example/model/             @ianshank
/example/requirements/      @ianshank
/example/evidence/          @ianshank

# The gate itself, and the policy it enforces.
/tools/archtrace/           @ianshank
/tools/tests/               @ianshank

# The controls around the gate: what CI runs, what the agents may do, what
# counts as a secret, and what the build is allowed to install.
/.github/                   @ianshank
/.pre-commit-config.yaml    @ianshank
/.gitleaks.toml             @ianshank
/Makefile                   @ianshank
/pyproject.toml             @ianshank
